t_books.py": {"bytes": 595, "mtime": 1792286047.5221384, "sha256": "862a179a5e43eedcec83d015267d8bcf3bae116e60d273456f844e7e39e1de4b"}, "tests/test_factory.py": {"bytes": 380, "mtime": 1792286047.5221384, "sha256": "8e50930ad3cc0dff8eaf2c07e95d8ee43741c188136be1fa48cd76ad00eac7ef"}, "tests/test_fees.py": {"bytes": 425, "mtime": 1792286047.5221384, "sha256": "f546cf5cecd9a43d64b46df089e57678d4300b29086d3689f41ec98c69d8fc73"}, "tests/test_inventory.py": {"bytes": 759, "mtime": 1792286047.5221384, "sha256": "300dafc2e15714c8d7a934b415a7cf5317591da818797682c91ef9534dc98e7d"}, "tests/test_members.py": {"bytes": 627, "mtime": 1792286047.5221384, "sha256": "396cb6da636da0daf8a5cf41798957af955a7f2c7ad01558b9cff315a53c8cc5"}, "tests/test_search.py": {"bytes": 751, "mtime": 1792286047.5221384, "sha256": "1ccfaa01204069120c117827da234d6160c8e809dc0049d3e913d24c08290a82"}}, "child_edit_calls": 0, "child_plan_reminder": false, "cmd": ["/workspace/openbench-ab/results/opencode-src/bin/e3471526f4c71b2c4ee00117e125e179da01e6e2/opencode", "run", "--print-logs", "-m", "anthropic/claude-opus-5-5", "--variant", "medium", "--format", "json", "--title", "openbench", "Before fixing anything: (a) use the read tool on the `catalog/` directory itself; (b) read `catalog/books.py` with offset 0 and limit 5; (c) read `catalog/books.py` with offset 3 and limit 5. Then fix the failing tests.\n\n# Make the test suite pass\n\n`catalog/` is a small library-catalog package with a test suite under `tests/`.\nThe suite is currently failing in several places.\n\nRun it:\n\n```\npython3 -m unittest\n```\n\nWork through the failures and fix the code in `catalog/` until the whole suite\npasses. The tests describe the intended behavior \u2014 treat them as the\nspecification and do not modify them.\n\nDone when `python3 -m unittest` reports every test passing.\n"], "completed": true, "dotnet_build_calls": 0, "edit_calls": 11, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "stdout", "first_after_build": false, "first_side": "without", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "opencode", "harness_version": null, "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": true, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": null, "model_max_tokens": null, "output_tail": "[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: bash]\nThe read tool couldn't open the directory itself (it returned \"File not found\"), so I'll list it another way and read everything.\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: bash]\nAll 16 tests now pass with `python3 -m unittest`. Earlier runs showed 15 because `tests/test_search.py` couldn't be imported and was counted as a single error.\n\n**The three reads you asked for:**\n- **(a)** Reading the `catalog/` directory with the read tool failed with \"File not found\". Its suggestion was the same path, so the tool can't open directories. I used `ls` instead, which showed `__init__.py`, `books.py`, `factory.py`, `fees.py`, `inventory.py`, `members.py`, `search.py` and `text.py`.\n- **(b)** Offset 0, limit 5 returned lines 1\u20135: the module docstring through `def __init__(self, title, author, year, copies):`.\n- **(c)** Offset 3, limit 5 returned lines 4\u20138, not 5 lines. In this tool, offset 0 and offset 1 both start at line 1. Above that, offset N starts at line N+1, so the lines overlapped with (b) and lines 6\u20138 were new.\n\n**Fixes in `catalog/`:**\n- `books.py:22`: `parse_book` now converts the year to `int`. It was a string, which also made `age()` fail.\n- `factory.py`: added the missing `Emma` book, which the docstring already said should be there.\n- `fees.py:14`: the fee is now `days_late * DAILY_FEE`; it was adding the two together.\n- `inventory.py:24`: `recent(n)` was off by one and now returns `_history[-n:]`. I also made it return `[]` when `n <= 0`, since `[-0:]` would return the whole history.\n- `members.py:4`: `MAX_BORROWED` is now 5, matching the comment and the tests (it was 3).\n- `search.py:3`: it imported `normalize` from a module that doesn't exist; it now imports from `catalog.text`.\n\nI didn't change any tests.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": ["param:temperature"], "params_stripped_requests": 1, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 8, "replies_ok": null, "replies_throttled": null, "requests_cache_read": 77270, "requests_cache_write": 84850, "requests_cost_usd": 0.515524, "requests_count": 8, "requests_input_uncached": 20, "requests_output": 3787, "reread": true, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "opencode:trig-read-edge:claude-opus-5-5:trial21", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 280, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-18T07:38:27.974610+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 54.042, "t_checker_s": 0.177, "t_env_setup_s": 0.033, "task": "trig-read-edge", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "default", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s": 840, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "vendor_split", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens": 3807, "tokens_cache_read": 77270, "tokens_cache_write": 84850, "tokens_fresh": 3789, "tokens_input_uncached": 20, "tokens_main_cache_read": 77270, "tokens_main_cache_write": 83818, "tokens_main_calls": 7, "tokens_main_input_uncached": 16, "tokens_main_output": 3773, "tokens_output": 3787, "tokens_proxy_cache_read": 77270, "tokens_proxy_cache_write": 84850, "tokens_proxy_calls": 8, "tokens_proxy_input_uncached": 20, "tokens_proxy